{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Contract/test card for RED-first implementation:\\n\\n- Authoritative contract: f789 description + prerequisite 9895 canonical disposition, 4a44 selection/cap policy, b69c status snapshot, 1104 pause CAS, and existing legacy facade tests.\\n- Public inputs: bridge_preview(*, only=None, exclude=None, repo_root=None); bridge_sync(*, only=None, exclude=None, max_changes=None, repo_root=None); bridge_status(*, target_environment_id=None, max_age_seconds=None, repo_root=None); bridge_pause(reason, *, repo_root=None); bridge_resume(*, repo_root=None); bridge_check_access(). Collection inputs are typed string lists; only/exclude are mutually exclusive; max_changes/max_age_seconds are positive integers when present. MCP mirrors these names except repo_root and never exposes mode.\\n- Outputs: typed schema-backed BridgeRun, BridgeStatus, BridgeControl, and BridgeAccessCheck results. Canonical operational/invalid outcomes raise RebarError (library) or the existing MCP error envelope with canonical returncode 1/2; benign dispositions remain typed successful results. Legacy reconcile(mode=...) and bridge_fsck retain exact signatures/results/errors/schemas.\\n- Happy tier: public library calls and real FastMCP registration/model boundaries with deterministic fakes only at Jira/network/time.\\n- Held-out edge tier: boundary validation, mutation-gate contrast (disabled/enabled and read-only), benign disposition rows, operational/invalid errors, pause idempotence, no-write collateral invariants, and legacy compatibility.\\n- Held-out E2E tier: real temp git refs/repos through public library and build_server().call_tool, compared with existing CLI semantics.\\n- CI gates: focused pytest nodes collected/executed under make test, plus schema generation/drift, lint, typecheck, module-size, and full CI.\\n- Contention exemption: adapters invoke one already-locked/CAS operation and add no retry/cache/check-then-act."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786396225888776001,"uuid":"6262adf1-f86f-4db8-b8b8-24c3b053eb84"}